<section class="cs-shell cs-continuity" aria-labelledby="cs-continuity-heading">
  <header class="cs-continuity-header">
    <div><p class="cs-kicker">PALIMPSEST // DHF CONTINUITY OFFICE // MODULE 1.7.0</p><h2 id="cs-continuity-heading">Continuity &amp; Psychosurgery</h2><p>GM-only console. The Fray track is an optional Cold Storage house rule, not a Core personality-fragmentation check.</p></div>
    <div class="cs-continuity-header-actions"><button type="button" data-action="openBook" aria-label="Open Cold Storage adventure book"><i class="fa-solid fa-book-open" aria-hidden="true"></i> GM Book</button><button type="button" data-action="review" aria-label="Preview changes to existing character sheets">Review World</button><button type="button" data-action="migrate" class="cs-primary">Apply Reviewed Migration</button></div>
  </header>
  <section class="cs-panel cs-continuity-help" aria-label="Core and house rule distinctions"><div class="cs-panel-head"><h3>Rule boundaries</h3><span>CORE 2020 / OPTIONAL FRAY</span></div>
    <p><strong>Official Core:</strong> resleeving loss is event-specific, not a tax for reaching sleeve five, six, seven or eight. Trauma, Personality Frag and Compromised DHF Baggage require a single starting choice: two Skill downgrades or EP2d6. Psychosurgery requires Virtual and is handled by the Altered Carbon Clinical Console. Baggage choices made here are the same record the character sheet shows, so a choice is never charged twice.</p>
    <p><strong>Cold Storage only:</strong> five scheduled memory pulses, two once-per-PC anchors, voluntary dangerous recall and a player-directed choice when Fray reaches six. The 110 years in inert storage are not subjective years in Virtual.</p>
    <p class="cs-hint">Back up the world before any migration. Book Only never rewrites actors. The continuity updater is separate, opt-in and skips a character who has switched to a different current sleeve.</p>
  </section>
  <div class="cs-continuity-grid" role="list">
  {{#each pcs}}
    <section class="cs-panel cs-continuity-pc {{#if active}}cs-continuity-active{{/if}}" role="listitem" aria-label="{{name}} continuity">
      <header class="cs-continuity-pc-head"><div><p class="cs-kicker">DHF // {{pcId}} {{#if active}} / SELECTED FOR PLAY{{else}} / PROTECTED RESERVE{{/if}}</p><h3>{{name}}</h3><p><strong>Sleeve #{{ordinal}}</strong> &middot; {{activeSleeveType}} &middot; {{confirmedSleeves.length}} confirmed earlier &middot; {{disputedArchives.length}} contested archives</p></div><span class="cs-ordinal">#{{ordinal}}</span></header>
      {{#if hasActor}}
      <div class="cs-continuity-stats" aria-label="Ego and Fray"><div><span>Fray <small>house rule</small></span><strong>{{#if optOut}}Not used{{else}}{{fray}} / 6{{/if}}</strong></div><div><span>Ego <small>Core resource</small></span><strong>{{ego.remaining}} / {{ego.recoverableMax}}</strong></div><div><span>Permanent loss</span><strong>{{ego.permanent}}</strong></div></div>
      {{#if ego.critical}}<p class="cs-continuity-danger" role="alert">Ego is zero. Stop routine Fray escalation; agree a Core p.147 continuity / treatment ruling with the player.</p>{{else}}{{#if ego.fragRisk}}<p class="cs-continuity-danger" role="alert">Permanent Ego loss exceeds remaining Ego. GM adjudicates Trauma Loop / Personality Frag under Core p.147.</p>{{/if}}{{/if}}
      <div class="cs-continuity-controls"><button type="button" data-action="optOut" data-pc="{{pcId}}" data-enabled="{{optOut}}">{{#if optOut}}Enable optional Fray{{else}}Opt out of Fray{{/if}}</button><button type="button" data-action="clinical" data-pc="{{pcId}}"><i class="fa-solid fa-heart-pulse" aria-hidden="true"></i> Clinical Console</button><button type="button" data-action="recordTreatment" data-pc="{{pcId}}">Record clinical outcome</button></div>
      {{#unless optOut}}
      <div class="cs-continuity-section"><h4>Five scheduled continuity pulses</h4><p>Ask the player. Stay Present rolls <strong>Composure</strong> in realspace or <strong>Discipline</strong> in Virtual; difficulty D0 at Fray 0-3, D1 at 4-5. Veiling a scene never costs resources.</p>
        <div class="cs-continuity-buttons">{{#each pulses}}<button type="button" data-action="pulse" data-pc="{{../pcId}}" data-pulse="{{id}}" {{#if resolved}}disabled{{/if}} title="{{label}}">{{#if resolved}}<i class="fa-solid fa-check" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{else}}<i class="fa-solid fa-circle" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{/if}} {{label}}</button>{{/each}}</div>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-continuity-section"><h4>Grounding and fracture</h4><div class="cs-continuity-buttons">{{#each anchors}}<button type="button" data-action="anchor" data-pc="{{../pcId}}" data-anchor="{{id}}" {{#if used}}disabled{{/if}}>{{#if used}}Used: {{else}}Anchor: {{/if}}{{label}}</button>{{/each}}</div>
        <div class="cs-continuity-controls"><button type="button" data-action="overreach" data-pc="{{pcId}}">Voluntary deep recall (high risk)</button><button type="button" data-action="fracture" data-pc="{{pcId}}" {{#unless atFracture}}disabled{{/unless}} class="cs-critical-button">Fracture at Fray 6</button></div>
      </div>
      {{/unless}}
      {{#if baggage.length}}<div class="cs-continuity-section"><h4>Official starting Baggage</h4><p>Resolve once per Item, only if the starting character has not already paid its cost. EP alternatives are recoverable unless another official event makes loss permanent.</p><div class="cs-continuity-buttons">{{#each baggage}}<button type="button" data-action="baggage" data-pc="{{../pcId}}" data-bag="{{id}}" {{#if resolved}}disabled{{/if}} title="{{choice}}">{{name}} {{#if resolved}}(recorded){{else}}(choose ruling){{/if}}</button>{{/each}}</div></div>{{/if}}
      <p class="cs-continuity-foot">{{fractures}} resolved fractures &middot; {{treatments}} recorded treatment decisions. All historical body counts are narrative records; no earlier deaths are automatically charged again.</p>
      {{else}}<p>Full-import this pregen into a fresh world to enable checks and treatment links. Book Only will not create or rewrite a player character.</p>{{/if}}
    </section>
  {{/each}}
  </div>
  <p class="cs-hint">The original 160 relationship links and existing handout permissions are retained. Two legacy sleeve dossiers are contested Palimpsest records rather than additional confirmed worn bodies. This console stores GM-only history and does not broadcast secrets to players.</p>
</section>
